(852428, 96580, 24240, '<td valign="top">I like this photo! It has a number of things going for it.  First, it reflects the rule of thirds in a number of ways including space devoted to  textures, space devoted to colors, and foreground vs background space. Together they create a nice rythym as well as balance throughout the whole.  I like the way the viewer can see the water from the side; also the sharp contrast the black badkground provides for the complementary shades of flesh vs medium blue. The action goes well with the title.  Lovely foot model.  Criticism:  I would like to see the top cropped ever so slightly...not a lot, to perfect the balance.</td>', 'I like this photo! It has a number of things going for it.  First, it reflects the rule of thirds in a number of ways including space devoted to  textures, space devoted to colors, and foreground vs background space. Together they create a nice rythym as well as balance throughout the whole.  I like the way the viewer can see the water from the side; also the sharp contrast the black badkground provides for the complementary shades of flesh vs medium blue. The action goes well with the title.  Lovely foot model.  Criticism:  I would like to see the top cropped ever so slightly...not a lot, to perfect the balance.', '2004-08-10 12:07:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(852433, 96536, 24240, '<td valign="top">Intersting idea and the perfect gunmetal blue. I would suggest cropping the top to focus more on the feet unless you could reshoot, in which case, try varous angle scenarios almost ground level with the feet.</td>', 'Intersting idea and the perfect gunmetal blue. I would suggest cropping the top to focus more on the feet unless you could reshoot, in which case, try varous angle scenarios almost ground level with the feet.', '2004-08-10 12:12:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(852443, 96151, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice bw, great contrast.  focus could be a little sharper.  good job with a tough handheld shot, finding the right mix between av and tv in order to get enough light for all the details without too much washout and without blurring due to a slower shutter speed.</td>', 'nice bw, great contrast.  focus could be a little sharper.  good job with a tough handheld shot, finding the right mix between av and tv in order to get enough light for all the details without too much washout and without blurring due to a slower shutter speed.', '2004-08-10 12:23:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(852447, 96459, 23394, '<td valign="top">great capture!  timing and patience pays off.  there''s a lot to be said for being in the right place at the right time, and having practiced enough to be able to take advantage of an opportunity.  i hope you do well with this!</td>', 'great capture!  timing and patience pays off.  there''s a lot to be said for being in the right place at the right time, and having practiced enough to be able to take advantage of an opportunity.  i hope you do well with this!', '2004-08-10 12:26:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(852448, 96533, 24240, '<td valign="top">Nice colors.  I love the green under the feet and the way the dark brings up the light .  Maybe a little too close up though.  Back off just a little to more closely follow the rule of thirds in balancing out background vrsus foreground and light versus dark.  Great title and conveyed well by the the picture which showsthe feet hovering.  The texture of the stone is shown to advantage.</td>', 'Nice colors.  I love the green under the feet and the way the dark brings up the light .  Maybe a little too close up though.  Back off just a little to more closely follow the rule of thirds in balancing out background vrsus foreground and light versus dark.  Great title and conveyed well by the the picture which showsthe feet hovering.  The texture of the stone is shown to advantage.', '2004-08-10 12:27:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(852456, 96492, 23394, '<td valign="top">great...now i have to go and unsubmit my vp entry...lol.<br/> <br/>kind of hard to shoot this and for it to come out not so centered...unless you had a tripod and a remote release.  <br/> <br/>also, for grins, you could rig a cheap throwaway camera with a remote release to catch a real train coming through, print it out, then incorporate that into your shot.  yeah, the effort involved would probably not be justifiable...but it could make a killer image &lt;g&gt;.</td>', 'great...now i have to go and unsubmit my vp entry...lol. kind of hard to shoot this and for it to come out not so centered...unless you had a tripod and a remote release.   also, for grins, you could rig a cheap throwaway camera with a remote release to catch a real train coming through, print it out, then incorporate that into your shot.  yeah, the effort involved would probably not be justifiable...but it could make a killer image <g>.', '2004-08-10 12:33:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(852458, 95556, 23394, '<td valign="top">nice idea, but the image is too small and the lighting could use some work.</td>', 'nice idea, but the image is too small and the lighting could use some work.', '2004-08-10 12:35:32.000000', NULL, 1),
